NVIDIA userspace utilities and libraries 615.71.09 (Arch-style
"nvidia-utils") for the Gaming Live CD, split out of the main Nvidia driver
package.

Contents:
- 64-bit libraries in /Programs/Nvidia-Utils/lib: the glvnd stubs (libGL.so.1,
  libEGL.so.1, libGLESv1_CM.so.1, libGLESv2.so.2, libGLX.so.0, libGLdispatch,
  libOpenGL.so.0, libOpenCL.so.1), libcuda + libcudadebugger, libnvcuvid,
  libvdpau_nvidia, libnvoptix and the whole libnvidia-* family (89 files).
- 32-bit libraries in /Programs/Nvidia-Utils/lib32 (61 files). TRANSITIONAL:
  these belong to Lib32-Nvidia-Utils; they stay here for now so the 32-bit
  Steam client and 32-bit games keep working until that recipe lands.
- Tools in /Programs/Nvidia-Utils/bin: nvidia-smi, nvidia-xconfig,
  nvidia-modprobe, nvidia-debugdump, nvidia-persistenced, nvidia-powerd,
  nvidia-cuda-mps-control/-server, nvidia-pcc, nvidia-ngx-updater and
  nvidia-bug-report.sh. (nvidia-settings is NOT here; it lives in the
  Nvidia-Settings recipe.)
- NVNGX/DLSS Wine DLLs (_nvngx.dll, nvngx.dll, nvngx_dlssg.dll) under
  lib/nvidia/wine.
- Vulkan ICD registration: /usr/share/vulkan/icd.d/nvidia_icd.json plus the
  absolute-path nvidia_icd.x86_64.json / nvidia_icd.i686.json and
  nvidia_icd_vksc.json; /usr/share/vulkan/implicit_layer.d/nvidia_layers.json.
  The absolute paths point at /Programs/Nvidia-Utils/Current/lib{,32} so
  Proton's bwrap sandbox loads this program's libGLX_nvidia.so.
- glvnd EGL external platforms (bundled in the .run, so no separate
  egl-wayland / egl-wayland2 / egl-x11 recipes): registered in
  /usr/share/glvnd/egl_vendor.d/ as 09_nvidia_wayland2.json,
  10_nvidia.json, 10_nvidia_wayland.json, 15_nvidia_gbm.json,
  20_nvidia_xcb.json, 20_nvidia_xlib.json, with the .so.1 sonames pinned by
  post_install for both architectures.
- OpenCL ICD (etc/OpenCL/vendors/nvidia.icd), the udev load rule
  (etc/udev/rules.d/60-nvidia.rules), the modprobe blacklist
  (etc/modprobe.d/nvidia.conf), the Xorg OutputClass configs
  (usr/share/X11/xorg.conf.d/10-nvidia.conf and nvidia-drm-outputclass.conf),
  the nvidia-dbus policy and the application profiles.

Ownership: kernel modules, the Xorg DDX (nvidia_drv.so +
libglxserver_nvidia.so), nvidia-settings and the GSP/ucode firmware come from
the Nvidia recipe. This recipe needs no kernel
headers and compiles nothing - it unpacks the same .run as Nvidia and copies
the userspace payload out.
